Execute the playwright tests: npx playwright test

Creating the test file in playwright:
Demo.spec.ts ==> spec: specification i.e testing purpose
			Ts: typescript file
We need to import 2 functions test and expect from @playwright/test

Execute test from particular file in headless mode: npx playwright test demo.spec.ts 
Execute test from particular file in actual browser: npx playwright test demo.spec.ts --headed
 npx playwright test demo.spec.ts --project=chromium
npx playwright test demo.spec.ts --project=chromium --headed

Explanation of the Results which are generated after execution
Running 1 test using 1 worker
Worker means: Helper or assistant which helps to execute scripts for you
You -> Worker 1 , Friend -> Worker 2
100TCs are split between as 50, 50

Playwright assigns the workers to the execution based on your computers CPU power

But we can also use the worker as per our need


npx playwright test --workers=3     Running 9 tests using 3 workers ==> Parallelism
npx playwright test demo.spec.ts --headed --workers=3      
npx playwright test demo.spec.ts --headed --project=firefox --workers=3
			
LOCATORS:
PLAYWRIGHT RECOMENDED
page.getByRole:
Use page.getByRole for buttons, checkboxes, radiobuttons, links and  inputTextFields and it should have Role attribute and it should have clear and visible text-Label and area-label .
	
	Await page.getByRole('role',{name : 'textvalue'}).fill('Laptop');
	Await page.getByRole('searchbox',{name : 'Search Amazon.in'}).click();
	
	<button type="submit" class="a-button-text" alt="Continue shopping">Continue shopping</button>
	Await page.getByRole('button',{name : 'Continue shopping'})

page.getByText:
Select based on the Visible Text, for the elements which are enclosed in <a> tag or <span> tag. The elements which have open and closed tags
await page.getByText('visible Text');
await page.getByText('Keep Shopping for')

page.getByLabel():
We can use it when we have label tag and for attribute:
<label for="name" class="col-sm-3 col-form-label">Name:</label>
await page.getByLabel('Name:')

page.getByPlaceholder()
We can use for the input fields by there placeholder text.
await page.getByPlaceholder('name@example.com')

page.getByAltText()
We can use for the fields by there alt text.
await page.getByAltText('Refrigerators').click();

Page.getByTestId()
We can use for the attribute by there data-testid value.
await page.getByTestId('main-menu-trigger').click();

Page.getByTestId()
We can use for the attribute by there title value.
await page.getByTitle('Keep selected tool active after drawing — Q').click();

CSS LOCATORS
1.Tag	Page.locator("tagName")
2.id	Page.locator("#idName")
3.class	Page.locator(".className")
	HTML==> Class="className1 className2 className3"
	Page.locator(".className1.className2.className3")
4.attribute	Page.locator("tagName[attribute='value']")

XPATH LOCATORS
1.By Attribute	Page.locator("//tag[@attribute='value']")
2.By Text	Page.locator("//tagName[text()='value']")



RECORDING SCRIPTS IN PLAYWRIGHT AND CODEGEN FUNCTIONS

npx playwright codegen ==> launches playwright inspector
npx playwright codegen https://www.amazon.in/
npx playwright codegen https://www.amazon.in/ --output=tests/demo2.spec.ts ==> records steps and copy to a file
npx playwright codegen https://www.amazon.in/ --viewport-size="800, 600"  ==> sets the size of the browser window.
npx playwright codegen https://www.amazon.in/ --device="iPhone 12" ==> Emulation of various devices
